<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kumbakonam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kumbakonam is a temple town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, between the Kaveri and Arasalar rivers. An important centre under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaks</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> of Thanjavur, it is known for its many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temples and for the Mahamaham festival, held at its sacred tank every twelve years. It was long a centre of learning.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kumbakonam.jpg" alt="Kumbakonam" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Trawell.in · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kumbakonam_Mahamaham_Tank.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
